# What never reaches the Docker daemon.
#
# Two jobs. The first is speed: without this the build context is the whole
# working tree — .venv/ and frontend/node_modules/ alone are hundreds of
# megabytes, uploaded on every single build.
#
# The second is the one that actually matters. Nothing in the Dockerfile copies
# `.env` today, but a build context that *contains* a live credential is one
# careless `COPY . .` away from an image that ships it, and images get pushed to
# registries. Excluding it here means the secret cannot reach the daemon at all,
# so no future edit to the Dockerfile can leak it by accident.

# --- secrets: the reason this file is not optional ------------------------- #
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
frontend/.env.local

# --- version control ------------------------------------------------------- #
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- Python build and tool state ------------------------------------------- #
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
dist
build
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# --- not part of the runtime image ----------------------------------------- #
# The tests are excluded on purpose: the runtime image should not carry the
# fixtures, and `make test` runs against the working tree, not the image.
tests
frontend
docs
doc
Makefile
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
fly.toml
README.md
CLAUDE.md
